<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    MikeOS ROM — repo local manifest.

    Place this file at .repo/local_manifests/mikeos.xml in your LineageOS 23.2
    source checkout (see README build runbook), then `repo sync`.

    What it does: adds the proprietary Google vendor blobs for tegu (Pixel 9a)
    from TheMuppets, which are NOT part of the open LineageOS manifest. These
    are the closed-source hardware bits (graphics, camera HAL, modem, etc.) the
    device needs to boot — they are firmware, NOT Google apps, and do not make
    the ROM "Googled".

    NOTE — vendor/mikeos is deliberately NOT a project here. This repo
    (mikeos-rom) is cloned/symlinked directly into the tree at
    /srv/src/vendor/mikeos by build-tegu.sh; it is not fetched by repo. Keeping
    it out of the manifest means `repo sync` never touches or clobbers it.

    KNOWN-UNVERIFIED (see README):
      * Canonical blob route is `breakfast tegu`, which makes roomservice fetch
        the LineageOS device/kernel trees, and the device tree's extract-utils /
        proprietary-files.txt then either pulls blobs from a connected/stock
        image OR from TheMuppets. If breakfast already wires the tegu vendor
        (many devices ship a matching TheMuppets entry in the default Lineage
        manifest / roomservice), this explicit project may be redundant or even
        conflict — in that case remove it. Verify the exact `name` and `path`
        against TheMuppets/proprietary_vendor_google @ lineage-23.2:
          - repo name : TheMuppets/proprietary_vendor_google
          - for tegu the blobs live under vendor/google/tegu
        Adjust `path` if the branch lays them out differently.
-->
<manifest>

  <!-- Proprietary Google hardware blobs for tegu (Pixel 9a). -->
  <project
      name="TheMuppets/proprietary_vendor_google"
      path="vendor/google"
      remote="github"
      revision="lineage-23.2" />

</manifest>
